State of New York { Dutchess County ss. }
On this ninth day of June one thousand eight hundred and thirty eight personally appeared before me Daniel D. Stein a Judge of the court of Common Pleas of said County of Dutchess Margaret Van Vleck a resident of the Town of La Grange in said County aged eighty one years, who being first duly sworn according to Law doth on her oath make the following declaration in order to obtain the benefit of the provision made by the act of Congress passed July fourth one thousand eight hundred and thirty six - That she is the widow of Abraham Van Vleck, who was a private soldier in the militia of the State of New York and served in the revolutionary army and was a pensioner under the act of June second one thousand eight hundred and thirty two and that he had in his possession at the time of his death a Certificate of pension given at the war office of the United States the twenty fifth day of October one thousand eight hundred and thirty three of which the following is a true Copy -
War department revolutionary claim - I certify that in conformity with the law of the United States of the 7th. June 1832 Abraham Van Vleck of the State of New York, who was a private in the revolutionary army is entitled to receive fifty five dollars and seventy five cents per annum during his natural life, commencing on the 4th. of March 1831 and payable semiannually on the 4th. of March and 4th. of September in every year Given at the war office of the United States this 25 day of October one thousand eight hundred and thirty three. Genl. Cass Secretary of war Examined and Countersigned J. S. Edwards Commissioner of Pensions. She further declares that she was married to the said Abraham Van Vleck

