State of North Carolina } County of Orange }
March On this 31 st day of A. D. eighteen hundred and fifty five personally appeared before me a Justice of the Peace within and for the County and State aforesaid Elizabeth Tilley aged about Fifty Four years a resident of the County of Orange and State of North Carolina who being duly sworn according to law, declares that she is the widow of Lazarus Tilley who was a private soldier in the Revolutionary War but she cannot give the names of any of his officers, the length of his service, nor when nor where he entered the service; but he was a pensioner of the United States at the rate of Thirty dollars per annum. She further swears that she is now a pensioner of the United States at the rate of Thirty dollars per annum, that her certificate of Pension bears date at the Department of the Interior on the 21 st day of September 1852, and is numbered 4523, said certificate was issued under act of Feb 3 rd 1853
She further swears that she was married to the said Lazarus Tilley in Orange County North Carolina, on or about the 18 th day of April A. D. 1829 by one William Horner a Justice of the Peace and that her name before her said marriage was Elizabeth Edwards. That her said husband died in Orange County North Carolina on or about the 3 rd day of

Buffalo N.Y. January 30 1845 J. L. Edwards Esq. } Commissioner of Pensions } Washington }
Dear Sir
I am sorry to trouble you again in relation to the Application of Lydia Hall for a pension as the former Widow of Israel Meade - I received a certificate of Pension granting $25.63. per annum. I have been unable to ascertain how that amount was fixed upon as her pension. I was in doubt whether the amount of Pension was discretionary with the Commissioner or the Secretary of War. I had supposed that if she was entitled to any thing she would be entitled to a full pension Widow's pension - "She was married before the expiration of the last period of his service" This inquiry may be in bad taste - but after diligent inquiry and examination I am unable to ascertain why she is not entitled to a full pension. Her friends inquire of me but I am unable to give any satisfactory answer - They are

State of New York } County of Yates Co. }
On this Eighth day of July 1843. before me Augustus Torrey The Subscriber a Justice of the peace for Said County of Yates personally appeared Mary Shipman who on her oath declares that she is the same Mary Shipman who was and is the widow of George Shipman. and to whom a Certificate of Pension was issued under the Act 7th July 1838 for five years from the Sixteenth day of February 1838 at the rate of Eighty Dollars per Annum, but to cease on the day of the Marriage or Death of the Said Widow. Payment to be made at Detroit by E P Hastings, Esq. agent for paying pensioners in the State of Michigan, from whence she has lately removed, that she now resides in the town of Middlesex in the Said County of Yates and State of New York where she intends to remain and wishes her pension to be there payable in future. That the Said Applicant has not drawn any money or received any pay on her Certificate since September 1841. The following are her reasons for removing from the town of Pittsfield Wastenaw County — and State of Michigan to the Said town of Middlesex in the Said State of New York. Middlesex was the place of her former residence and where she has a son and other friends residing and where she buried her late husband
Mary Shipman
Sworn and Subscribed to before me } the day and Year aforesaid }
Augustus Torrey J.P. }
State of New York } Yates County }
§§§
John C Strong of Gorham Ontario County being duly Sworn Saith that he is personally acquainted with Mary Shipman the above affiant and that the person who has taken the above oath is the person described in the above affidavit. and further this deponent Saith not Subscribed and sworn before me the 8th day of July 1843. and I further certify that the Said John C Strong is known to me and is a person of veracity Augustus Torrey J.P. }
John C. Strong

